A||||4||Homicidal||Sort of Fiero related: VERY strange CD-Changer problem!!!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||06-01-2001||06:23 PM||||I figured since the changer is in my Fiero, it's Fiero related!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Anyways, I have a strange problem with my cd changer.  Every once and a while when I play a cd (usually after I shut the car off and start agan) the right speakers becomes really fuzzy, like a bad radio signal sound.  Happens in the headrest speakers and I think the dashboard speaker too.<P>If I play the CD Cleaner I have in my car (which I keep in there all the time now) and then re-play the cd, it will go away.<P>I would assume it's a REALLY dirty lens, but I don't understand why it happens sporadically like this.  And I really don't understand why it happens after I turn the car off and on again, or if the car has been sitting.  Especially if I used the cd cleaner over and over.  <P>I notice that as I insert the Changer magazine into the changer, I hear the static coming through the speakers.  <P>Any ideas where to start on this?  Need more info?  Any help is appreciated!<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>It's sad, in the 20th Century, in the 1990's, we would have to still go the same bullshit route<BR>that artists have to go, to get acceptance.  If it wasn't for the independence, if it wasn't for the <BR>small little cities, and the few little ghetto guys, trying to make music, it never would have happened.<BR>Some of these guys will never make a dime, some of thse guys will be poor and die, alone.  <P>But in the proccess, they've been the true renegades.<P>And the true rebels always walk alone anyways.</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||06-01-2001||07:41 PM||||Where is the CD changer located? Is it properly ventilated? If it's in an area that gets hot and cold, (like behind a seat) it could get hot when you first power it on and cause condensation inside the unit. Then when you run the CD cleaner thru it, it removes the moisture. How long have you had the changer? If you've had it a while, It might be beneficial to pull it out, CAREFULLY remove a cover and see how much dirt, hair, and dust is inside of it. Make sure any vent holes are also clean. I would also get a lint free cloth and wipe the laser lens off. Remember to wipe it front to back. (from center hub towards outside edge)<BR>Don't wipe it side to side.<BR>Also don't try to move any of the mechanics of the changer. ("Hey whats this gear for?")<BR>I know it's a guy thing to fiddle,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> but if you mis-align the laser head it's a bear to get it back into alignment.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||SPDFREK||06-01-2001||07:59 PM||||What kind of changer is it? direct conect to the head unit, or a broadcast type? either way, I had the same problem with the first one I ever installed, It had a bad ground.<P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||1
Z||000003||Homicidal||07-05-2001||04:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Where is the CD changer located? Is it properly ventilated? If it's in an area that gets hot and cold, (like behind a seat) it could get hot when you first power it on and cause condensation inside the unit. Then when you run the CD cleaner thru it, it removes the moisture. How long have you had the changer? If you've had it a while, It might be beneficial to pull it out, CAREFULLY remove a cover and see how much dirt, hair, and dust is inside of it. Make sure any vent holes are also clean. I would also get a lint free cloth and wipe the laser lens off. Remember to wipe it front to back. (from center hub towards outside edge)<BR>Don't wipe it side to side.<BR>Also don't try to move any of the mechanics of the changer. ("Hey whats this gear for?")<BR>I know it's a guy thing to fiddle,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> but if you mis-align the laser head it's a bear to get it back into alignment.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The changer is behind my seat, it gets moderate to low ventilation, not much I can do on that area......I've had it for a good almost 2 years now....it might be due for an extensive cleaning.  <P>It's direct link.  As for the ground, I don't see a ground wire on there, just one wire running from the changer to the headunit.<P>I know it's the changer because the sound is perfect when playing a CD from the headunit or the radio.  <P>------------------<BR><B>It's sad, in the 20th Century, in the 1990's, we would have to still go the same bullshit route<BR>that artists have to go, to get acceptance.  If it wasn't for the independence, if it wasn't for the <BR>small little cities, and the few little ghetto guys, trying to make music, it never would have happened.<BR>Some of these guys will never make a dime, some of thse guys will be poor and die, alone.  <P>But in the proccess, they've been the true renegades.<P>And the true rebels always walk alone anyways.</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||07-05-2001||09:54 AM||||Hey Homi, think you could make your signature a little longer?  I like the fact that you already post it repeatedly in the same thread, but some more boring crap to scroll past would be heplful. Thanks buddy!<P>PS, about the cd player, sounds like it's time to can it before it starts gobbling discs. Welcome to the wonderful world of designed obsolesence.||||reg||1
